<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Read</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>read &lt;number&gt;
read &lt;thing&gt;
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>read 42
read note
</pre>
<p>With a number, read shows that message on the board in the room (see 
<a cmd='#'>Help Boards</a>); look at the board first to see its list of messages. On a 
competition board, it shows that competition instead.
</p><p>With anything else, read works like look at: read a note, a sign, a book 
or a scroll's writing just by naming it.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Boards</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Look</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Write</a>
</pre>




</div>